# 10. Inline-button/deep-link problem worth fixing

`send_to_channel()` currently creates the `"پست ناشناس"` button with **both**:

```python
url=...
callback_data=...
```



Telegram's current Bot API specifies that an `InlineKeyboardButton` uses **exactly one** type field other than the display fields. A URL button and callback button are distinct button types. [Telegram](https://core.telegram.org/bots/api%20?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

There are also several legacy routing inconsistencies:

```text
post_callback_handler → expects "post"
send_to_channel       → creates "post:<...>"
handle_post_callback  → expects "post_<...>"
```

and `direct_to_message_py_answer()` expects `answer_to_reply...`, while `get_inline_buttons()` generates `answer:` / `reply:`.

So for the new feature, callback/deep-link formats should be defined once and tested centrally.

